#: includes/configs/settings.php:28
msgid "Delivery"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:29
msgid "How notifications reach people: live updates while they browse, push notifications when the site is closed, and the bell in your header."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:34
msgid "Check For New (seconds)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:35
msgid "How often an open page looks for new notifications, so they appear without a refresh. Clear the box to check only when a page loads. Checking pauses while a tab is in the background and reads a single cached value, so the default of 60 costs almost nothing."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:44
msgid "Push Notifications"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:45
msgid "Send push notifications"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:46
msgid "Reaches people even when your site is closed, the way a phone app would. Your site must use HTTPS. The security keys are created for you the first time, so there is nothing to set up."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:53
msgid "Ask After (visits)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:54
msgid "How many visits before someone is asked to allow push notifications. Asking on a first visit is usually refused, and a refusal cannot be undone by you, so waiting a few visits gets far more people saying yes."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:64
msgid "Header Bell"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:65
msgid "Show a bell in the site header"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:66
msgid "Adds a bell with an unread count and a dropdown of recent notifications. Works with ListingHive and any theme built on HiveTheme. If your header has no bell after switching this on, your theme does not provide the area it hooks into."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:72
msgid "Bell Icon"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:73
msgid "Start typing to search, such as \"inbox\" or \"envelope\". If your theme trims Font Awesome down, an icon it no longer includes will not show."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:89
msgid "Bell Size (px)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:90
msgid "The size of the bell icon. The circle around it grows to match."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:100
msgid "Nudge Sideways (px)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:101
msgid "Shifts the bell left or right without moving anything else in your header. Use a negative number to move it left, a positive one to move it right. Only needed if the bell does not quite line up with the buttons beside it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:111
msgid "Nudge Up or Down (px)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:112
msgid "Shifts the bell up or down without moving anything else in your header. Use a negative number to move it up, a positive one to move it down."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:122
msgid "Bell Colour"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:123
msgid "The colour of the bell icon when nobody is pointing at it. The unread count on the bell has its own colour, under Appearance."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:131
msgid "Bell Colour (Hover)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:132
msgid "The colour of the bell icon while the pointer is over it. Leave it empty to keep the colour above."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:139
msgid "Bell Background"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:140
msgid "The circle behind the bell icon. Leave it empty for no circle, which suits most headers."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:147
msgid "Bell Background (Hover)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:148
msgid "The circle behind the bell while the pointer is over it. Leave it empty for a soft shade that works on light and dark headers alike."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:155
msgid "Hide Combined Counter"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:156
msgid "Hide the combined count beside the account name"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:157
msgid "HivePress adds unread messages, unpaid bookings and pending orders into one number beside the account name. The bell already covers those same events, so leaving both on shows people two counts for the same thing."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:164
msgid "Hide Messages Counter"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:165
msgid "Hide the unread count beside Messages"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:166
msgid "The separate count the Messages extension shows on its own menu item. Worth keeping, because it says how many unread messages there are specifically, which the bell does not. Hide it only if you would rather people used the bell alone."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:173
msgid "Sticky Header"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:174
msgid "Keep the header on screen when scrolling"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:175
msgid "Keeps the bell reachable on long pages. Leave it off if your theme already does this, or you will end up with two headers fighting each other."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:183
msgid "Count how many notifications are sent and opened"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:184
msgid "Anonymous totals per notification type, on the <a href=\"admin.php?page=hp_notification_stats\">Statistics</a> page. A notification counts as opened when someone follows it; simply marking it read does not count. Nothing about individual people is stored."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:193
#: includes/configs/settings.php:199
msgid "Pop-ups"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:194
msgid "The small cards that slide in to announce a notification while someone is browsing."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:200
msgid "Show new notifications as pop-ups"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:201
msgid "Turn this off and notifications still arrive; they simply wait in the list and on the bell instead of announcing themselves."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:208
msgid "Position"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:209
msgid "Which corner pop-ups appear in on desktops and laptops."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:217
msgid "Top Right"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:218
msgid "Top Left"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:219
msgid "Bottom Right"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:220
msgid "Bottom Left"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:225
msgid "Position on Mobile"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:226
msgid "Phones use this instead. Pop-ups span the full width on a small screen, so only top, middle or bottom makes sense there."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:234
msgid "Top"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:235
msgid "Centre"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:236
msgid "Bottom"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:241
msgid "Maximum Pop-ups"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:242
msgid "How many pop-ups can be on screen at once. Any others wait their turn rather than piling up."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:253
msgid "Hiding"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:254
msgid "Hide pop-ups automatically"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:255
msgid "Untick to leave pop-ups on screen until they are closed by hand."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:263
msgid "Hide After (seconds)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:264
msgid "How long a pop-up stays before hiding itself. Pointing at a pop-up pauses the countdown, so nobody loses one mid-read."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:275
msgid "Sound"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:276
msgid "Play a sound with pop-ups"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:277
msgid "Browsers only allow sound after someone has clicked somewhere on the page, so the first pop-up of a visit may be silent. Later ones will chime."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:284
msgid "Sound Style"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:285
msgid "Which tone plays when a pop-up arrives."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:297
msgid "Chime"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:298
msgid "Ping"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:299
msgid "Pop"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:300
msgid "Bell"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:301
msgid "Soft"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:308
msgid "Appearance"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:309
msgid "Colours and sizing, applied everywhere notifications appear: pop-ups, the bell dropdown and the notifications page."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:314
msgid "Background Colour"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:315
msgid "The background of pop-ups and the bell dropdown."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:322
msgid "Text Colour"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:323
msgid "The main text colour. Keep it readable against the background above."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:330
msgid "Accent Colour"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:331
msgid "The stripe down the side of each pop-up, the dot marking an unread notification, and the icon behind each one. Your brand colour usually suits."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:338
msgid "Corner Radius (px)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:339
msgid "How rounded the corners are. Set 0 for square corners, or clear the box to inherit whatever your theme uses."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:348
msgid "Text Size (px)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:349
msgid "The size of notification text wherever it appears."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:358
msgid "Text Weight"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:359
msgid "How bold notification text is. Unread notifications are always shown bolder than read ones, whichever you pick."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:366
msgid "Normal"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:367
msgid "Medium"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:368
msgid "Semi-bold"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:369
msgid "Bold"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:374
msgid "Unread Count Colour"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:375
msgid "The small number shown on the bell and beside Notifications in the account menu. Leaving this alone matches the counts HivePress already shows elsewhere."
